- No. No, there's no need.

115
00:04:41,106 --> 00:04:42,815
They got married. We saw them get married.

116
00:04:42,816 --> 00:04:44,317
- It was on TV. We all saw it.
- Yeah.

117
00:04:44,318 --> 00:04:48,404
Yes, yes, we saw it, but, uh, I need
the official marriage certificate,

118
00:04:48,405 --> 00:04:50,907
so I can prove they were actually married.
I mean, I have this.

119
00:04:50,908 --> 00:04:53,159
- Oh, then that's it. That's the one.
- That's great. Use it.

120
00:04:53,160 --> 00:04:55,912
Okay, uh, but see, this has
Frank's signature and thumbprint.

121
00:04:55,913 --> 00:04:58,623
It doesn't have Sam's signature
or thumbprint.

122
00:04:58,624 --> 00:04:59,916
I'm sorry.

123
00:04:59,917 --> 00:05:03,544
I-I can't help you guys unless I get
a signed copy with a thumbprint.

124
00:05:03,545 --> 00:05:05,796
- No! That can't be.
- It's okay, Dee.

125
00:05:05,797 --> 00:05:08,257
- Here you go.
- Can I just see the one that...

126
00:05:08,258 --> 00:05:11,220
Oh, j... Oh, you know... Oh, my God.

127
00:05:11,845 --> 00:05:16,098
This is my... Ah, fiddlesticks.
You know, I-I-I screwed this up.

128
00:05:16,099 --> 00:05:17,850
- Did you?
- I screwed the pooch on this one.

129
00:05:17,851 --> 00:05:20,144
Yeah, I botched it
'cause I brought the wrong paperwork.

130
00:05:20,145 --> 00:05:22,063
- You did?
- I have the marriage certificate

131
00:05:22,064 --> 00:05:24,357
that has been signed and thumbprinted
by both of them.

132
00:05:24,358 --> 00:05:25,733
- You do?
- I have it at my place.

133
00:05:25,734 --> 00:05:27,568
And we're gonna go get it
and bring it back

134
00:05:27,569 --> 00:05:29,529
- and all will be well in the world.
- Great.

135
00:05:29,530 --> 00:05:31,030
- I got it. I have a plan.
- Uh-huh.

136
00:05:31,031 --> 00:05:32,114
All right. Hey, hey, hey,

137
00:05:32,115 --> 00:05:34,075
when you come back,
can you bring me a cup of water?

138
00:05:34,076 --> 00:05:35,701
Charlie turned all the water off
down here.

139
00:05:35,702 --> 00:05:37,955
- Uh, water.
- Is that a yes?

140
00:05:38,747 --> 00:05:40,081
This is gonna work.

141
00:05:40,082 --> 00:05:42,792
Dad always knew
exactly what to do in a jam,

142
00:05:42,793 --> 00:05:45,753
and I think once he sees
your beautiful face,

143
00:05:45,754 --> 00:05:47,506
he's gonna think of something quick.

144
00:05:49,550 --> 00:05:51,300
Right. Uh, speaking of which,

145
00:05:51,301 --> 00:05:53,803
um, I don't think
he's gonna do this for nothing,

146
00:05:53,804 --> 00:05:58,642
so I was hoping maybe we could offer him
a conjugal visit for motivation?

147
00:05:59,434 --> 00:06:00,727
No way.

148
00:06:01,562 --> 00:06:04,689
Mommy, listen, we have to start acting
like a family again,

149
00:06:04,690 --> 00:06:06,274
otherwise this is not gonna work.

150
00:06:06,275 --> 00:06:09,318
Dad, Dad, hi! Hi, Dad.

151
00:06:09,319 --> 00:06:13,864
Hey, Dad. Dad. Dad. Hi, Dad.
Yeah, you have to put the phone to your...

152
00:06:13,865 --> 00:06:15,408
Dad, hi, how are you?

153
00:06:15,409 --> 00:06:19,328
Um, it's been a minute since we've seen
each other, um, you know, since the dance.

154
00:06:19,329 --> 00:06:21,497
You know, you...
you walked out early on that,

155
00:06:21,498 --> 00:06:24,458
so, um, just wasn't sure if you had
to, like, use the bathroom or...

156
00:06:24,459 --> 00:06:25,460
Did you like it?

157
00:06:26,336 --> 00:06:27,337
No.

158
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:31,507
No. No.
But you knew what I was going for, right?

159
00:06:34,303 --> 00:06:36,262
Oh. Express.

160
00:06:36,263 --> 00:06:38,055
Um, we've got a problem.

161
00:06:38,056 --> 00:06:40,766
Um... ...it appears
that Charlie's mom died,

162
00:06:40,767 --> 00:06:43,437
which means Mom is now
gonna be homeless.

163
00:06:45,188 --> 00:06:46,189
And?

164
00:06:47,566 --> 00:06:51,193
Well, and we were hoping
that you could help us out.

165
00:06:51,194 --> 00:06:54,238
You see...
...Dennis doesn't want Mom living with us

166
00:06:54,239 --> 00:06:56,949
and Charlie is gonna sell the house

167
00:06:56,950 --> 00:06:59,952
